{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ReebLinkingCwfNormalization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ReebLinkingCwfNormalization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Units","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.amplitude_bond_criticality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.amplitude_bond_criticality","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reeb-linking-cwf-normalization.lean#L52-L67","doc":"**Conditional on `ReebLinkingCWF`** — at the Markov bond factor\n`z = t⁻¹` (with `t = [2]_v` a unit) the amplitude satisfies the\ndeformed-criticality equation `g²·(1 + t²) = 1`: the conjectural CWF\namplitude lands exactly on the marginal-stability point of\n`ReebPnMagnitude.ss_det_zero_at_criticality`.\n\n§7c: `t : Kˣ`, so `t⁻¹` is the ring element `↑t⁻¹` and the old hypothesis\n`t ≠ 0` is carried by the unit itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.amplitude_normalized","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.amplitude_normalized","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reeb-linking-cwf-normalization.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Unit-tangent (CWF) normalization, square-root free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.amplitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.amplitude","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reeb-linking-cwf-normalization.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The linking amplitude as a function of the bond factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reeb-linking-cwf-normalization.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ReebLinkingCWF","kind":"class","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reeb-linking-cwf-normalization.lean#L41-L50","doc":"**Conjecture (CWF linking normalization).**  A linking-amplitude\nassignment on bond factors whose square is the unit-normalized transverse\ncomponent: `ℓ(z)²·(1+z²) = z²` for every bond factor `z`.  The physical\nclaim is that the Reeb linking amplitude of the pn bond is this `ℓ`\nevaluated at the Markov bond factor.  No instance is provided (open). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:reeb-linking-cwf-normalization","label":"conj:reeb-linking-cwf-normalization","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reeb-linking-cwf-normalization.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}